Dennom the Ranger was doing the long walk from the VS up to
DL1. Well, actually he was trying to use up his 40 odd
?oTeleport and 5c!oGL so they wouldn't go to waste. He was
procrastinating in trimming his load until he could visit
all his stashes so he was, of course, burdened.

On about DL20 he ran across a vampire lord that wouldn't get
out of the way. With +7 Frost Brand and -41 AC he didn't
even drop his bag except for a (m)mf, a disenchanter or an
L. Well the VL read a c?oCreateMonster, Rodney appeared and
summoned a titan, an umber hulk, a mmf and a black dragon
among others. It seemed like it happened all in one turn.

This is my worst nightmare. An umber hulk in a crowd, so I
can't rely on all my resources while the various nasties,
who wouldn't normally be any problem, all get to nibble at
me while I try to get control of the situation.

First things first, the /oDeath took out Rodney and the poor
floating eye that was in between. Whoops, now the umber hulk
got me with his gaze. Maybe the blindfold should have been
first. On goes the blindfold and it took two applications of
the unihorn. Now where did that mmf go? Hmmm... must have
been a doppleganger, or it got in front of the black dragon
at the wrong time.

Whack the umber hulk, and again. Why isn't he dead? Oh, I've
still got the +2 Magicbane wielded! Finish off the umber
hulk. By now the titan has summoned a couple more groups to
the party. I haven't had a titan for a pet since 3.3
something. So I killed two or three monsters to get next to
the titan, dropped the bag and the amulet and started
casting charm monster. Must have tried six or seven times
before he gave in.

Now while I'm killing a Nazgul, my titan, Goliath, gets
killed by an iron golem! No problem, there's a /oUT in the
bag. Let's just finish this Nazgul first. Whoops, Beauty, my
new black dragon, just ate Goliath's corpse! Sigh, and the
Nazgul zapped a /oDig and escaped!

Well, I guess I'll take my other new pets, Alex the Aleax
and Lestat the VL, and go. Beauty would just slow us down
with all that eating.

Stay tuned, Dennom was last seen on DL1 at 1:30 this morning
sorting through mounds of way too much really good stuff.

